an old stamped generation opens as a cache miss: true
an old stamped generation looks up as a miss the lookup decided, not a refusal: true
a lookup leaves every old-regime entry in place: true
a lookup changes no entry and leaves the old stamp as it was: true
a committed store and an admitted lookup are recorded, neither as a refusal: true
the store sweeps every old-regime entry: true
the store's completed sweep atomically advances the regime stamp: true
a current entry remains readable across later cache opens: true
an unstamped legacy generation looks up as a miss, left whole and unstamped: true
a store sweeps an unstamped legacy generation and stamps it current: true
a future regime refuses an otherwise readable entry: true
a regime-refused lookup and store are each recorded as a refusal: true
a refused future-regime open changes no entries: true
a refused future-regime open does not rewrite its stamp: true
a lookup in a directory not yet created is a miss, not a refusal: true
a call without a key does no I/O and records nothing: true
a store whose commit the filesystem refused is recorded as a refusal, with its reason: true
the refused commit leaves the earlier entry in place: true
a read of an existing entry the filesystem refused is recorded as a lookup refusal: true
an entry that fails to decode is a miss the lookup decided, not a refusal: true
a refused lock is recorded as a refusal of both a store and a lookup: true
recordings nest: the inner one sees its own I/O: true
recordings nest: the outer one sees the inner one's I/O too: true
